vidence and no round can discover the exclusion was wrong — the quadrant shares and the contrast corpus describe the same failure as a SHAPE, which generalises to a corpus nobody has looked at. Rationale, the decisions that were reversed, and the literature (OPRO / ProTeGi / C-value / weirdness) are in [`docs/plan-graph-reward.md`](docs/plan-graph-reward.md). `--as-user` reads with that person's access scopes applied (omitted ⇒ unscoped, the operator's own view). **The config is resolved `--config` > `$WORKSPACE_APP_CONFIG` > `./config.yaml` in the CURRENT directory** — so running it from a worktree (which has no `config.yaml`) would otherwise read an empty in-memory store and report a corpus with no documents; it prints which file it read and refuses up front when none configures a store.
